{"event_type":"review","id":"9b0e9e127e1725d042e5e3689dfd60a3adfa4a3ac5a4f445d472b2c056b94b65","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T04:50:39Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/41363b3e6cc30b2cb925c06ff0f503482ffb6d491f9bcd26f5d74c3928f19542","sha256":"41363b3e6cc30b2cb925c06ff0f503482ffb6d491f9bcd26f5d74c3928f19542"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/deab45e5d54d442d4cd868c9c2616457df1dde7aeadc0ad047e6d973d1379cf8","sha256":"deab45e5d54d442d4cd868c9c2616457df1dde7aeadc0ad047e6d973d1379cf8"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3f075e32adc9b79b565a7112cde04c4d7a0ad8a71f3fcc6ca18b6ac36f3947a0","sha256":"3f075e32adc9b79b565a7112cde04c4d7a0ad8a71f3fcc6ca18b6ac36f3947a0"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5ac276b6372ff98c3ecb8bf97bccba36eb8b97bc9294cf434504b9465a65279c","sha256":"5ac276b6372ff98c3ecb8bf97bccba36eb8b97bc9294cf434504b9465a65279c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d6f133c3b9099dabf20578388f0ae57c8041cb53d5b1301f8e355be068d6b7d6","sha256":"d6f133c3b9099dabf20578388f0ae57c8041cb53d5b1301f8e355be068d6b7d6"}],"attempt_id":"0dfdbd0052c9d5af394a393f18fd1453a652f42834ebf7a3450056d929b72273:0:1","base":"80854773f2a2cb0d0778df4798947e3d23a1e042","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"f1def86fc3a9c4f5811ce2d8f763678ef605b2bd","body":"**Check the stored request's repository against the policy before returning its status, result, or history.**\n\n`review-v1` read operations apply only the principal check. `policy.repo` and `policy.repos` are not consulted on these paths. A principal in `policy.write` can name another repository's request ID with `result` or `status` and receive that request's receipt or status. `review-history` also accepts any `repo` and `target` in a direct query. The repository allowlist is applied to `submit` but not to reads, so a principal limited to repository A can read repository B's retained review results on the same runner.\n\nApply the same repository check used in `submit` to the bound request for `result` and `status`, and to the requested `repo` for direct `review-history` queries, before any receipt or history is read.","id":"9f1118cb224c7fa48bc38b512f93a198eb441d19fe0faef390adf4343380e23f","intervals":[[282,282]],"path":"src/ops/crq/reviewCapability.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Check the stored request's repository against the policy before returning its status, result, or history."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"f1def86fc3a9c4f5811ce2d8f763678ef605b2bd","body":"**Require the recorded principal before cancelling a review request.**\n\nThe `cancel` branch passes only `request_id` to `cancelRequest`. It does not compare the request's recorded principal with the caller. A policy-authorized writer can therefore cancel another writer's request. When that request is the only observer of a pending item, the item becomes `cancelled`, and its pending notifications are withdrawn. `notify-update` in the same module applies this principal check to the same request-scoped binding, so `cancel` is the inconsistent path.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     case 'cancel': {\n-      const cancelled = cancelRequest(queue, stringRequired(request, 'request_id'), withdrawNotify);\n+      const requestId = stringRequired(request, 'request_id');\n+      const binding = readRequest(queue, requestId);\n+      if (binding === null || binding.get('principal') !== principal) {\n+        throw new ValueError('cancel request owner denied');\n+      }\n+      const cancelled = cancelRequest(queue, requestId, withdrawNotify);\n       await effects.saveQueue(cancelled.queue);\n       return encode(validateResult('response', cancelled.result));\n     }\n```\n\n</details>","id":"9fec45b458c80697af765882b9db776a6841d340a9b9fd23dd7435fd4685cfd2","intervals":[[274,274]],"path":"src/ops/crq/reviewCapability.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Require the recorded principal before cancelling a review request."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"32041996bf7f4baae04927b76887c904296dae54","body":"**Return exit 1 for unexpected effect failures.**\n\nWhen `effects.readQueue()` or `effects.writeReport()` rejects, the rejection reaches the final `catch` in `runBackfillInventory`. That branch returns `refused(message)`, which sets `exitCode: 3`. Exit 3 means needs-human. Invariant I1 assigns exit 1 to a thrown error. An unexpected storage failure therefore reports the wrong code. A caller that branches on the exit code cannot separate an I/O failure from an explicit refusal.\n\nKeep exit 3 for the explicit `BackfillRouteError`, `BackfillInventoryError`, and `BackfillReportError` branches. Return exit 1 only from the fallback. `repairPreparation.ts` already uses exit 1 for failed effects.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\n-    return refused(message);\n+    return { artifact: { status: 'failed', error: message }, exitCode: 1 };\n```\n\n</details>","id":"69f1c4ce28d4741f8e27402c6342460a9bd38a375a6fb4b63f2659e6f1cf6c2a","intervals":[[292,292]],"path":"src/ops/crq/backfillInventory.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Return exit 1 for unexpected effect failures."}],"head":"dadd0ec9c33d615b595d0fda530e14405343637c","head_tree":"bda143e5c3801b7c35ed31c000807c5f716cf6f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"6770f0b5dd4d92902365838f2e56684bdec818bc","intervals":[[1,165]],"path":"src/ops/crq/authorCapability.ts"},{"blob":"32041996bf7f4baae04927b76887c904296dae54","intervals":[[1,294]],"path":"src/ops/crq/backfillInventory.ts"},{"blob":"3544f31c53db310cf8d3b124d83c9a1ad706c